WEBVTT

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.240
Ta-da!

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.040
Why are you dressed like that?

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.080
Vacation! Vacation!

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.790
Why are you saying "vacation?"

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.340
What?

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.010
Have you not told the Vice Commander yet, Hana?

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.760
I told her.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.340
I told her there'd be no Orgone energy movement for the next three days...

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.010
And so we're going on vacation!

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.230
Aren't you always going to the pool and eating sweets while on the job, anyway?

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.140
Those aren't vacations... Those are breaks!

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.020
Lately, we've had nothing but tough missions.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.240
And sleeping in a train car every night really makes my shoulders stiff...

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.740
Don't you understand the situation we're in?

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:57.990
That's what I'm saying.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.290
We don't know what tomorrow will bring,

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.830
so we need to enjoy ourselves while we can.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.370
Don't you agree, Captain?

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:13.170
Well, if we were normal students,
we would be on summer break right now...

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.130
But given what's going on...

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.020
True, you guys may need a break.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.020
Fine.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.270
I'll give the Midsummer's Knights clearance for a vacation.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.280
Us, too?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.030
Just make sure that we can reach you at any time, okay?

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.070
Pitz, she says we're going on vacation!

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.450
All right!

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:48.420
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:55.550
I'm watching an endless dream

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:02.010
Aren't you watching too?

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:09.350
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:16.190
Can't you see it too?

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.700
The things you can't normally say

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.370
The things you try to express

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.870
The things you're willing to fight for

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:32.590
Standing on your own two feet

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:39.260
The night sky illuminates them all

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:46.390
The first flash of lightning

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:52.730
This is our battle to fight

00:02:53.400 --> 00:03:00.070
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:08.580
This dream will absolutely come true

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.920
They're ready for use.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.800
You fixed them up, huh?

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.260
They're perfect!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.340
That was faster than expected.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.800
We worked hard.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.850
Don't forget to give us that data!

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.850
You were the one who said

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.350
we should leave the Machine Goodfellow testing to Amara and Moco, Pac.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.360
But the development schedule is lagging badly behind.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.320
The pilot's mental state

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.450
greatly affects the Neural Maneuver System's capabilities.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.580
The test method we're currently using is the best way to obtain the data we need.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.120
When humanity goes to space as part of the Kivotos Plan,

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.710
that system will be necessary.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.840
Is it falling behind because they're slacking,

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.430
or because they're uncooperative?

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.930
I have no data on that.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.220
We must do something.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.640
Aren't there any measures we can take

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.400
that would allow us to control people more directly?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:23.320
I suppose you're the only one at the company who I can truly control...

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:29.160
Do not forget that I have your emergency shutdown switch.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.910
Pac does not lie.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.710
Even if the Machine Goodfellows have been repaired...

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.880
...we don't have Setsuna's capsule anymore.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.970
The new engine series is finally nearing completion.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.890
It'll be great to have a spare.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.310
Once this new model is complete,

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.360
both it and the Nebula Engine will be a great help.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.530
But in the scenario you're foreseeing,

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.860
this will do more than merely enhance our interception capabilities, correct?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.080
What has Alonzo said about our plan?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.660
They're still running the numbers.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.500
Give them a little more time.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.560
My, my... For the first time in ages, we get to sleep in actual beds!

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.270
Well, just remember to exercise restraint.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.110
You're in the room next to mine?

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:59.830
I can't believe I have this huge room to myself!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.810
Hana?!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.730
The rooms are connected? No, wait...

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.690
They're the same room?

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:30.570
This is just one room with two entrances!

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.080
I think that they're called adjoining rooms.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.700
A-Adjoining rooms?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.410
Adjoining rooms!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.590
You set us up, didn't you, Akari?

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.920
I'm all sweaty.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.760
What?!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.840
I'm going to take a bath.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.220
A bath...

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.730
Calm down!

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.940
Calm down, Captain!

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.090
"Hey, Akari... This isn't funny!"

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.340
"Hana and I in the same room?
You can't do that!"

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:37.770
I'd expected him to come say something like that, but...

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.730
What do you do on vacation?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.350
Captain?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.560
Y-Yes?

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.070
Goodnight.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.940
G-Goodnight...

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.340
Hana?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.420
What's wrong?

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.200
Are you crying?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.650
Well, how did it go?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.900
How did what go?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.070
I exercised restraint.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.530
Restraint?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.160
Yes, restraint...

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.780
I exercised perfect restraint!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.450
Really?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.410
Really.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.540
Really?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.960
Are you talking about last night?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.040
Did something happen?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.380
"Not a thing," he says...

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.920
Why?

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.680
"Why"?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.220
I'm not sure,

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.760
but I think she might hate me.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.560
Hate you? Hana?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.270
She hates you?

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:36.440
Miss, have you ever considered modeling?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.200
No photographs!

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.530
Just one...

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.700
Come with me, Hana!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.530
Wait...

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.080
Of course she doesn't hate you.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.080
When you go to sleep before she does,

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.380
she often goes over to kiss you.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:16.070
Hey, Hana...

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.400
You want to get some ice cream?

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:20.110
Sure!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.780
Do you like ice cream?

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.330
Yep.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.330
Do you prefer mint chocolate chip or vanilla?

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.920
I like both of them...

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:34.750
But if I had to choose... Mint chocolate chip?

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.840
Then, mint chocolate chip or the captain?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.210
The captain!

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.590
Yeah, I thought so...

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.230
Wait.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.980
They're still underage.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.030
Perhaps I had overestimated you...

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.830
I have received yet another complaint from Technology and Research Division 3.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:18.090
Evidently you deployed several Machine Goodfellows without permission, and got them destroyed.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:24.510
You also used our Orgone energy capsules, didn't you?

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.760
Those are an extremely valuable energy resource.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:30.470
A single capsule is capable of powering even the latest in mobile weaponry models for decades.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.690
What did you use them for?

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:37.270
What could you have possibly done to drain a capsule completely?

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.820
The two of us fought a mock battle.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.070
It was part of our pilot training.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:46.660
We thought improving our skills would benefit the company.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:47.280
You're wasting my time.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.410
The Neural Maneuver Systems need

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.250
to be tailored to a specific individual, or any actions are pointless.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.750
The Machine Goodfellows are not your toys!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.880
From this point onward, you are forbidden from using them without clearance.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:05.220
And you are to obey Technology and Research Division 3.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.220
Understood?

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.390
Do not disappoint me.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.230
Welcome, Lady Malkin, Lord Amarok.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.990
I don't think we need Kube Masaki anymore.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.410
He's obnoxious.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.370
My projections suggest that we may need Kube Masaki for a while longer.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:36.710
Eliminating him now will make exercising control over Macbeth Enterprises significantly more difficult.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:41.500
When a man who's only lived for a few decades tries to treat me like a child,

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:44.210
it irritates my real self more than anything!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.260
Kube Masaki still has his uses.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:53.430
Globe's Independent Attack Force stationed in Tanegashima is a much more immediate problem.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:59.730
Thus far they have disrupted all of our attempts to initiate an abreaction via Machine Goodfellow.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.110
I am well aware of that.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.480
I know!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.320
I've got a great idea.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:19.460
This satellite, Legacy, was made by the Seton Company as part of Kube's plan.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.920
The stock satellite Kube built for the escape into space,

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.470
that's halfway between the Earth and Moon?

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.930
I'd rather not waste food...

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.930
But if we dropped the Legacy on Tanegashima...

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.560
It'd blow the island away, and also cause problems for Kube.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.190
Two birds with one stone?

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:45.780
I like it.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.990
You can do it, can't you, Pac?

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.990
Understood.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.990
Eyecatch

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:05.750
Did you know that there's a total lunar eclipse tonight?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.470
I worked so hard to arrange a romantic setting for them...

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.760
I guess they're still just kids.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.680
Hana was born of my race...

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.600
So I think she has the same nature...

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.060
The same peculiarity, you might say.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.570
When we kiss someone,

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:32.490
we can feel what they're thinking, to an extent.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.030
A kind of telepathy?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:35.950
Yeah.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.490
A telepathic kiss.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.710
Telepathic kiss?

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:46.420
Now that I think about it, I did feel like I got a glimpse into her mind for a moment...

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:55.350
Wait a second, doesn't Hana only kiss the captain when he's asleep?

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.100
If Hana does have that peculiarity...

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.630
Why are you crying?

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:40.640
Hana?

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.100
I thought I should just kill you...

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.320
I...

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.110
I love you, Daichi.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.710
I want to kiss you, Hana.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:13.800
I can't...

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:15.880
I can't!

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:21.220
If you knew my real self...

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:24.430
You'd hate me!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.820
An emergency call?

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.990
Yes? This is Manatsu!

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.320
We have an emergency!

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.490
Midsummer's Knights, get over here right now!

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.580
Sir! It's an emergency!

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.080
What's going on?

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.210
The Seton Company's modified asteroid in orbit around L1,

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:56.050
the Legacy, has fired its engines!

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.680
It's currently accelerating toward Earth.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:09.480
It's been a little over twelve hours since Legacy went out of control.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.770
It's less than a hundred meters in diameter.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:16.530
Something that small can't be detected by the space guard's early warning system!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:20.490
Legacy is going to crash into Earth?

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.490
Legacy sighted.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.750
Verifying predicted point of impact.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.500
I've got it.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.880
It's the south end of Japan... Tanegashima!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:32.710
What?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.670
Less than seven minutes to impact!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:39.510
The Legacy satellite weighs around 100,000 tons.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:44.970
If it crashes, the resulting energy expenditure will measure in the megatons.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.690
This base... No, all of Tanegashima will be obliterated!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.900
Is this a deliberate attack?

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:58.360
The Legacy is our stockpile satellite. It's where we've kept the materials needed for the Kivotos Plan.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.610
Who's behind this?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:05.450
The Legacy appears to have been set on a course to strike Tanegashima.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.790
They're after the Globe base?

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.210
Likely, yes.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.830
What's going on?

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.390
No one can stop it now.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:23.720
The low-orbit Impactors?

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.970
Citronnier is the closest!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.480
It won't be able to intercept in time.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:35.570
A 100,000-ton satellite is heading straight toward Tanegashima.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:36.820
Can we intercept?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.070
It's already moving at six kilometers per second...

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:44.070
With that much kinetic energy, even if we destroy it,

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.990
it won't change the damage it does!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:48.700
Commander...

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:59.300
Tell the staff in the underground blocks to remain there!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.260
Is there no way to evacuate the civilians?

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.510
150 seconds to impact!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.390
There's no time!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:10.810
Hana!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.370
What?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:40.960
I'm detecting a high-intensity heat source coming from the Tanegashima coast!

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.550
The <i>Blume</i>?

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.810
The Legacy satellite has been destroyed.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.530
The <i>Blume</i>'s beam weapon?

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.530
The <i>Blume</i>?

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:47.780
Did the <i>Blume</i> do that?

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:51.120
Now you've done it, Princess...

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:54.120
Thank goodness...

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.620
That was the <i>Blume</i>'s Orgone beam.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.840
Then Hana did this?

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:21.820
Hana...

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:28.570
I'm not the girl you think I am.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:30.910
Hana?

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:31.910
Stay back!

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:35.000
Hana!

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:42.000
Hana...

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:15.800
Hana runs away from us,

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:17.640
and by chance, finds Setsuna in the city.

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:23.020
Amara and Moco from the Planetary Gears find her.

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:26.150
Run, Hana! They're after you!

00:24:26.150 --> 00:24:32.070
Big changes are coming for Hana, Setsuna, and Macbeth Enterprises.

00:24:32.070 --> 00:24:35.280
Next time, on episode 15 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:37.030
True Self.

00:24:37.030 --> 00:24:39.870
Earth Engine, scramble!
